{
  "info": {
    "name": "Signa API - Course Tracking",
    "description": "Auth + catalog + course-tracking (enroll, block interactions) flow against a local signa-api instance (docker compose, local profile). Content fixtures reference the LSA / basic-course YAML seeded by ContentImportRunner.\n\nRun order matters: folders are numbered and must run top to bottom. The email-verification step needs a token pulled from the `tokens` table (local SMTP isn't reachable from an automated runner) — see that request's description.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "test_email", "value": "newman.qa@example.com" },
    { "key": "test_username", "value": "newman_qa" },
    { "key": "test_password", "value": "Postman123!" },
    { "key": "verification_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "access_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "refresh_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "sign_language_id", "value": "2582ecea-37dc-4025-9dd1-99cb935c488b" },
    { "key": "course_id", "value": "c3d572cc-65f5-4f23-bccc-4b85f8632e51" },
    { "key": "course_version_id", "value": "ab746ce1-ec6e-489f-b1ae-2182b73aa299" },
    { "key": "topic_id", "value": "3c393c1b-b0be-48b5-bc78-617c52e2257d" },
    { "key": "lesson_id", "value": "ce98d4f5-2dee-4ccf-bd04-2fd27af4941a" },
    { "key": "info_block_id", "value": "f4339869-e009-4e22-a459-2282f85ec46b" },
    { "key": "select_meaning_block_id", "value": "90fbb7cb-f224-492a-afbc-d06641f23060" },
    { "key": "select_sign_block_id", "value": "eba0e809-df44-4d98-a60f-824360504970" },
    { "key": "match_block_id", "value": "cd687b6d-9a12-4d1d-955f-a3d9ebaf45ef" },
    { "key": "unknown_id", "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Auth - Register",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/register",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{test_email}}\",\n  \"username\": \"{{test_username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{test_password}}\",\n  \"name\": \"Newman QA\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register - Duplicate Email (409)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/register",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{test_email}}\",\n  \"username\": \"someone_else\",\n  \"password\": \"{{test_password}}\",\n  \"name\": \"Someone Else\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('Body reports email already in use', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('Email already in use');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - Before Verification (401, mislabeled)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"{{test_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{test_password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Documents an existing bug, not the intended behavior: AuthService.login() has an explicit `if (!user.isEnabled()) throw new InvalidCredentialsException(\"Account not verified\")` check, but it's unreachable. Spring Security's DaoAuthenticationProvider pre-auth checks (via CustomUserDetails.isEnabled() -> user.isEnabled()) reject a disabled account with a DisabledException before AuthService's own check runs, and GlobalExceptionHandler's generic AuthenticationException handler maps that to a plain 401 'Invalid credentials'. See the report."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('Body actually says Invalid credentials, not Account not verified', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('Invalid credentials');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Auth - Verify & Login",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Verify Email (dev-only token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/verify?token={{verification_token}}",
            "description": "In production the token comes from the link in the verification email. This harness has no mailbox access, so `verification_token` is pulled straight from the `tokens` table (type=EMAIL_VERIFICATION) for {{test_email}} right after the Register call and injected into the environment before this request runs."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"{{test_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{test_password}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has access_token and refresh_token', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.refresh_token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.environment.set('access_token', body.access_token);",
                  "pm.environment.set('refresh_token', body.refresh_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - Wrong Password (401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"{{test_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"WrongPass123!\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('Body reports invalid credentials', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('Invalid credentials');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/refresh",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refresh_token\": \"{{refresh_token}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response rotates both tokens', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.refresh_token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.environment.set('access_token', body.access_token);",
                  "pm.environment.set('refresh_token', body.refresh_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Catalog (read)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Courses Catalog",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/courses?signLanguageId={{sign_language_id}}",
            "description": "Query params are bound directly by Spring (camelCase), NOT through the snake_case Jackson strategy that request/response bodies use. Sending `sign_language_id` here 500s instead of 400ing — see the report."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('basic-course is in the catalog', () => {",
                  "  const ids = pm.response.json().content.map(c => c.id);",
                  "  pm.expect(ids).to.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('course_id'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Course Detail",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/courses/{{course_id}}"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Course has the expected single topic', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.topics).to.have.lengthOf(1);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.topics[0].id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('topic_id'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Lesson Content",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/lessons/{{lesson_id}}"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Lesson exposes its 4 blocks in order', () => {",
                  "  const blocks = pm.response.json().blocks;",
                  "  pm.expect(blocks).to.have.lengthOf(4);",
                  "  pm.expect(blocks.map(b => b.type)).to.eql(['INFO', 'SELECT_MEANING', 'SELECT_SIGN', 'MATCH']);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Course Tracking - Happy Path",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Enroll in Course",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/courses/{{course_version_id}}/enroll"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Enroll in Course - Duplicate (409)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/courses/{{course_version_id}}/enroll"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('Body reports already enrolled', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql(\"User is already enrolled in this course's version\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "View INFO block (first view, awards XP)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{info_block_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{}" }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "View INFO block again (repeat view, idempotent)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{info_block_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{}" }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Attempt SELECT_MEANING - incorrect (no XP)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{select_meaning_block_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"is_correct\": false\n}" }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Attempt SELECT_MEANING - correct (first correct, awards XP)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{select_meaning_block_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"is_correct\": true\n}" }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Attempt SELECT_MEANING - repeat correct (no double XP)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{select_meaning_block_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"is_correct\": true\n}" }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Attempt SELECT_SIGN - correct",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{select_sign_block_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"is_correct\": true\n}" }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Attempt MATCH - correct (completes lesson/topic/course)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{match_block_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"is_correct\": true\n}" },
            "description": "This is the last unresolved block in the only lesson of the only topic of the course, so it should cascade: lesson COMPLETED -> topic COMPLETED -> enrollment COMPLETED. Cascade outcome is verified directly against the DB (see report) since there's no read endpoint yet for enrollment/lesson/topic progress."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Course Tracking - Validation Errors",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Enroll - unknown course version (404)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/courses/{{unknown_id}}/enroll"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 404 Not Found', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test('Body reports course version not found', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('Course version not found');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Interaction - unknown block (404)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{unknown_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{}" }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 404 Not Found', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test('Body reports lesson block not found', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('Lesson block not found');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Interaction - INFO block with is_correct set (400)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{info_block_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"is_correct\": true\n}" },
            "description": "Single-DTO contract: the frontend doesn't need to know a block's resource type ahead of time, but the server still enforces it can't send a correctness value for an INFO block."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Body reports the INFO/correctness mismatch', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('INFO blocks do not accept a correctness value');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Interaction - evaluable block without is_correct (400)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{select_sign_block_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{}" }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Body reports the missing correctness value', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('This lesson block requires a correctness value');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Edge Cases",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Interaction without Authorization header (local profile)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/learning/tracking/blocks/{{select_sign_block_id}}/interactions",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"is_correct\": true\n}" },
            "description": "Documented as-is, not asserted as correct behavior: the `local` security profile permits every request through the filter chain, so this never gets the 401 a real deployment (`!local` profile, `.anyRequest().authenticated()`) would return. With no principal resolved, @AuthenticationPrincipal is null and the controller NPEs into a 500. See the report."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('local profile: no auth enforcement, principal is null, request 500s', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(500);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
